  a: addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(input:{pullRequestReviewThreadId:"PRRT_kwDORbZKrs6duQuw", body:"Valid, and mine — fixed in `742e4ea`.

This was collateral from the ADR status true-up earlier in this PR. DES-024 originally read `PROPOSED ... Pending security review discussion — deferred by CEO`, which was coherent. I flipped the status to SETTLED (the decryption path is implemented in `internal/pgp/decrypt.go`) and left the trailing sentence untouched, so the entry then asserted both that the decision was settled and that it was still pending.

Now reads: `Security review discussion deferred by the CEO; the decision itself is settled.` That separates the two facts the original wording had fused — the decision is made, a review conversation was deliberately deferred, and neither implies the other.

Worth noting the pattern, since this is the third instance in this PR: correcting a status or a section and missing a dependent sentence elsewhere. The other two were an overview paragraph still describing the old send-path behaviour, and a heading count that disagreed with its own table. Same shape each time — the fix lands, its restatement somewhere else does not."}){ clientMutationId }
}
